\]

We first define \(\lambda=r\frac{p}{1-p}\) (i.e., mean of the NB). Consequently, \(p\) can be expressed as \(\frac{r}{r+\lambda}\), and \(1-p\) is \(\frac{\lambda}{r+\lambda}\) \[
